{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timeout","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuspendingClock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"duration","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws before the first element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example","level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Throws","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeoutError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"customError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") when ","type":"text"},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" passes between elements, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any error the upstream throws.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock (","type":"text"},{"code":"ContinuousClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SuspendingClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") holds the one thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/timeout\/timeout(_:customerror:)"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"customError"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":")?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","text":"AsyncSequences"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","text":"Timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV","text":"SuspendingClock"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"TimeoutSequence.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/TimeoutSequence.swift#L176"},"externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE7timeout_11customErrorAA14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutVy_x12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockVGs8DurationV_s0F0_pSgtF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","extendedModule":"_Concurrency","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"